IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g7-commencement`
IMPORT `g8-fees`

-- int-commencement.l4: integration points IP2, IP13 and IP16, and headline (d): the commencement day and the dates of the
-- Fees Regulations.  This module belongs to the integration layer (the INTEGRATOR's); it is the only place where group 7's
-- commencement functions are fed group 8's date, and it is the only module that decides what "the facts as the sources give
-- them" are.  Nothing here reads a Hebrew text of its own: the dates are the sources' (the gazette dates are in the modules
-- of groups 7 and 8, which quote them).
--
-- What is decided here, and what is not.
--   IP13  the day the section 59 regulations came into force is group 8's reg.5 date (7 days from the publication of 9.7.2025,
--         which IL s.10(a) puts on 16.7.2025), handed to group 7's record of facts.
--   IP2   "the Law has commenced for the work on the system" is group 7's function of the system, the day and those facts.
--   IP16  "Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act" is group 7's function of the day and those facts.  It REFUSES from the
--         first day of the later limb of s.63(b) for as long as no regulation under s.46 is known: the sources contain none.
--   The day the Law was published in Reshumot is a constant of the Law (Sefer HaChukim 3349, 14.1.2025), not a fact of any case.
--   A regulation under s.46 is NOT in the sources; the facts "as the sources give them" therefore carry NOTHING for it, and the
--   alternative that supplies a date is a separate function, used by the tests with a stated hypothetical date.

§ `Integration points IP2, IP13, IP16 and headline (d): the commencement and the dates of the Fees Regulations`

§§ `The facts that fix the commencement`

@ref Law s.63(a)(1) (publication of Sefer HaChukim 3349, 14.1.2025); Fees Regulations as made, regulation 5 (IP13)
@desc The facts that fix the commencement of the Law as the sources give them: published 14.1.2025, the section 59 regulations in force from the date group 8 computes, and no regulation under section 46 in the sources
GIVETH A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63`
`int — the facts that fix the commencement, as the sources give them` MEANS
    `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63` WITH
        `the day the Law was published in Reshumot` IS YMD 2025 1 14
        `the s.59 regulations came into force on` IS `the Fees Regulations made under section 59 came into force on`
        `the day regulations under section 46 came into force, if any` IS NOTHING

@ref Law s.63(b), s.46(b); Fees Regulations as made, regulation 5
@desc The facts that fix the commencement of the Law on the assumption that regulations under section 46 came into force on the given day; the sources contain no such regulation, so the day is a hypothesis of the caller
GIVEN `the day regulations under section 46 came into force` IS A DATE @desc The day the regulations under section 46 are taken to have come into force
GIVETH A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63`
`int — the facts that fix the commencement, section 46 regulations being in force from` `the day regulations under section 46 came into force` MEANS
    `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63` WITH
        `the day the Law was published in Reshumot` IS YMD 2025 1 14
        `the s.59 regulations came into force on` IS `the Fees Regulations made under section 59 came into force on`
        `the day regulations under section 46 came into force, if any` IS JUST `the day regulations under section 46 came into force`

§§ `IP2 and IP16: the two booleans the other groups consume`

@ref Law s.63(a) (IP2)
@export Whether the Law has commenced, on the given day, for work on the given cooling system (section 63(a): from the commencement day for a lawful listed flammable refrigerant, 18 months later for any other); the facts that fix the commencement are those the sources give
GIVEN system IS A `Cooling system` @desc The system worked on: its capacity and the refrigerants it operates by
      day IS A DATE @desc The day of the work
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`int — the Law has commenced for work on the system on the day` system day MEANS
    `the Law has commenced for work on the system` system `on the day` day `given the facts` `int — the facts that fix the commencement, as the sources give them`

@ref Law s.63(a) (IP2)
@desc The same, on the stated facts that fix the commencement
GIVEN system IS A `Cooling system`
      day IS A DATE
      facts IS A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`int — the Law has commenced for work on the system on the day, given the facts` system day facts MEANS
    `the Law has commenced for work on the system` system `on the day` day `given the facts` facts

@ref Law s.63(b) (IP16)
@export Whether Chapter 6 (financial sanctions) was in force on the given day (section 63(b)); a named refusal while the sources show no regulation under section 46 and the first limb has run
GIVEN day IS A DATE @desc The day of the act
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`int — Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` day MEANS
    `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` day `given the facts` `int — the facts that fix the commencement, as the sources give them`

@ref Law s.63(b) (IP16)
@desc The same, on the stated facts that fix the commencement
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      facts IS A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`int — Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act, given the facts` day facts MEANS
    `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` day `given the facts` facts

§§ `Headline (d): the commencement day and the dates of the Fees Regulations`

@ref Law s.63(a)(1)
@export The commencement day of the Law (section 63(a)(1)): the later of three months from the publication of the Law and the day the section 59 regulations came into force
GIVETH A DATE
`int — the commencement day` MEANS
    `the commencement day under section 63(a)(1)` `int — the facts that fix the commencement, as the sources give them`

@ref Law s.63(a)(2)
@export The day the Law commences for work on a system with any other refrigerant (section 63(a)(2)): 18 months from the commencement day
GIVETH A DATE
`int — the day the Law commences for work on a system with any other refrigerant` MEANS
    `the day the Law commences for a system with any other refrigerant under section 63(a)(2)` `int — the facts that fix the commencement, as the sources give them`

@ref Law s.63(b), s.46(b)
@export The day Chapter 6 commences (section 63(b)): a named refusal, because it is the later of 18 months from the commencement day and the entry into force of regulations under section 46, and no such regulation is in the sources
GIVETH A DATE
`int — the day Chapter 6 commences` MEANS
    `the day Chapter 6 commences under section 63(b)` `int — the facts that fix the commencement, as the sources give them`

@ref Law s.63(b), s.46(b)
@export The day Chapter 6 commences if regulations under section 46 came into force on the given day: the later of that day and 18 months from the commencement day
GIVEN `the day regulations under section 46 came into force` IS A DATE @desc The hypothetical day the regulations under section 46 came into force
GIVETH A DATE
`int — the day Chapter 6 commences, section 46 regulations being in force from` `the day regulations under section 46 came into force` MEANS
    `the day Chapter 6 commences under section 63(b)` (`int — the facts that fix the commencement, section 46 regulations being in force from` `the day regulations under section 46 came into force`)

§§ `The owner's ruling on s.63(a)(1) (fork F-C-3 of group 7): the default stands, and the alternative is callable`

-- Ruled by the owner on 2026-10-14 (NOTES.md, "Owner rulings"): the default is the later of the two DATES (14.4.2025, three months from publication, and
-- 16.7.2025, the s.59 regulations), so day X is 16.7.2025.  The alternative reading is that "three months from" governs both limbs: three months from the
-- LATER of the two days, 16.7.2025, so day X is 16.10.2025.  The three functions below are the alternative; the headline functions above are the default.
-- Group 2 takes day X as an input date, so the alternative reaches the Second Schedule's three-year notes by passing it.

@ref Law s.63(a)(1) (fork F-C-3 of group 7)
@desc The commencement day on the alternative reading of s.63(a)(1): three months counted from the later of publication and the entry into force of the section 59 regulations (16.10.2025 on the facts of the sources)
GIVETH A DATE
`int (three months from the later of the two days) — the commencement day` MEANS
    `s 63(a)(1) — the commencement day, under the readings` `int — the facts that fix the commencement, as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates with the three months counted from the later of the two days`

@ref Law s.63(a)(2) (fork F-C-3 of group 7)
@desc The day the Law commences for a system with any other refrigerant on the alternative reading: 18 months from that commencement day (16.4.2027 on the facts of the sources)
GIVETH A DATE
`int (three months from the later of the two days) — the day the Law commences for work on a system with any other refrigerant` MEANS
    `s 63(a)(2) — the day the Law commences for a system with any other refrigerant, under the readings` `int — the facts that fix the commencement, as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates with the three months counted from the later of the two days`

@ref Law s.63(a) (IP2; fork F-C-3 of group 7)
@desc Whether the Law has commenced for work on the system on the day, on the alternative reading of s.63(a)(1)
GIVEN system IS A `Cooling system` @desc The system worked on: its capacity and the refrigerants it operates by
      day IS A DATE @desc The day of the work
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`int (three months from the later of the two days) — the Law has commenced for work on the system on the day` system day MEANS
    `s 63(a) — under the readings, the Law has commenced for work on the system` system day `int — the facts that fix the commencement, as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates with the three months counted from the later of the two days` `the readings of the regime taken`

@ref Fees Regulations as made, regulation 5 (IP13)
@export The day the Fees Regulations made under section 59 came into force: 7 days from their publication on 9.7.2025
GIVETH A DATE
`int — the Fees Regulations came into force on` MEANS
    `the Fees Regulations made under section 59 came into force on`

@ref Fees (Amendment) Regulations, Kovetz HaTakanot 12383; Interpretation Ordinance s.17
@export The day the 2026 amending regulations came into force: the day of their publication, since they state no commencement
GIVETH A DATE
`int — the amending regulations came into force on` MEANS
    `the 2026 amendment of the Fees Regulations came into force on`
